$ =====================================================================
$ RBE3 BUG TEST DECK B -- DX_BAR/DY_BAR/DZ_BAR self-coupling bug
$ (RBE3_PROC.f90, lines ~239-241 and ~315-420; NOT covered by issue #224)
$
$ Full 6-DOF RBE3 (REFC=123456) with 4 independent grids, each given
$ a DIFFERENT weight on its X, Y and Z translational components
$ (three separate WTi/Ci groups per grid below). This is the
$ "differential per-DOF weight" pattern that both the WRITE_L1J_456
$ bug (Deck A) and this DX_BAR/DY_BAR/DZ_BAR bug require to manifest.
$
$ The 4 independent grids are driven by SPC to the EXACT rigid-body
$ field  U_i = U0 + omega x r_i  for:
$     U0    = ( 0.37, -0.82,  1.15)
$     omega = ( 0.21, -0.44,  0.63)
$
$ Any correct weighted least-squares RBE3 fit MUST recover this U0
$ and omega EXACTLY at the reference grid, for ANY weights -- a rigid
$ field has zero fit residual regardless of weighting. This is
$ independent of (and additional to) the Deck A bug: even with
$ WRITE_L1J_456 fixed, this deck will still show a large error unless
$ DX_BAR/DY_BAR/DZ_BAR are also corrected to the full 6-term
$ cross-weighted sums described in the report.
$
$ Expected (correct formulation), grid 900:
$   T1=0.37  T2=-0.82  T3=1.15   R1=0.21  R2=-0.44  R3=0.63
$
$ Actual (as-coded, buggy), grid 900 (from an independent Python
$ re-implementation of RBE3_PROC.f90's exact formulas):
$   T1=2.409  T2=-0.071  T3=4.349   R1=1.051  R2=-5.492  R3=0.703
$ (off by roughly 1 to 6x on every component -- not a rounding-level
$ discrepancy)
$ =====================================================================
SOL 101
CEND
DISP = ALL
SPC = 1
BEGIN BULK
$
$ Reference (dependent) grid -- all 6 DOF dependent on the RBE3.
GRID,900,,0.,0.,0.
$
$ Independent grids.
GRID,901,,1.0,0.5,0.2
GRID,902,,-0.7,1.2,-0.3
GRID,903,,0.3,-0.9,1.1
GRID,904,,-1.1,-0.4,-0.8
$
$ Dummy grids + harmless CROD so the model isn't entirely empty.
GRID,800,,5.,5.,5.
GRID,801,,6.,5.,5.
MAT1,1,1.,,0.
PROD,1,1,1.
CROD,98,1,800,801
$
$ RBE3: reference grid 900, REFC=123456, independent grids 901-904,
$ each with a DIFFERENT weight per translational component
$ (Wx, Wy, Wz respectively) -- this non-uniform per-DOF weighting is
$ what exposes the bug; uniform per-grid weighting would mask it.
RBE3    10              900     123456  1.0     1       901     4.0     +A1
+A1     2       901     0.8     3       901     2.0     1       902     +A2
+A2     0.3     2       902     1.7     3       902     0.5     1       +A3
+A3     903     1.5     2       903     2.9     3       903     3.0     +A4
+A4     1       904     2.2     2       904     0.6     3       904
$
$ Independent-grid SPC values = exact rigid-body field
$ U_i = U0 + omega x r_i  for U0=(0.37,-0.82,1.15),
$ omega=(0.21,-0.44,0.63). Rotational DOF (4,5,6) fixed to zero
$ (unused by the RBE3's COMPS_I=123, but pinned to avoid singular
$ unconnected DOF).
SPC,1,901,1,-0.033
SPC,1,901,2,-0.232
SPC,1,901,3,1.695
SPC,1,901,456,0.
$
SPC,1,902,1,-0.254
SPC,1,902,2,-1.198
SPC,1,902,3,1.094
SPC,1,902,456,0.
$
SPC,1,903,1,0.453
SPC,1,903,2,-0.862
SPC,1,903,3,1.093
SPC,1,903,456,0.
$
SPC,1,904,1,0.974
SPC,1,904,2,-1.345
SPC,1,904,3,0.582
SPC,1,904,456,0.
$
$ Dummy CROD grids, fully fixed.
SPC,1,800,123456,0.
$ (grid 801 deliberately left unconstrained -- gives the model a
$  genuine free DOF so MSC Nastran has an L-set to solve; it's an
$  unloaded dummy CROD end, disconnected from the RBE3 under test, so
$  this has no effect on the RBE3 results.)
$
ENDDATA
